# Testing

Full conventions, including sections not live yet (GraphQL mocking,
`test-utils/interactions`), live in `TESTING.md` at the repo root. This is
the condensed, must-follow subset for what's actually installed today.

## Query selector priority (use in this order)

1. `getByRole("button", { name: "Submit" })`
2. `getByLabelText("Email")`
3. `getByPlaceholderText("Enter email")`
4. `getByText("Welcome")`
5. `getByDisplayValue`, `getByAltText`, `getByTitle`
6. `getByTestId` — avoid unless absolutely necessary

## Naming

`describe("ComponentName")`, `it("does X when Y happens")` — no generic
names like `"Render"` or `"Works"`.

## Interactions

`@testing-library/user-event` isn't installed — use `fireEvent` from
`@testing-library/react` directly. Do not add `user-event` to reach for it;
that's a `TESTING.md`-tracked "planned" swap, not a default.

## Chakra-rendering components

Wrap with `Provider` from `@/components/ui/provider`, not a one-off
`ChakraProvider`. See `CreateAccountForm.test.tsx` for a working example.

## Test data — never real contact details

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
const mock = { phone: "07911 123456", email: "jane.doe@gmail.com" };

// ✅ GOOD — reserved test ranges
const mock = { phone: "07700 900123", email: "jane.doe@example.com" };
```

Phone: UK Ofcom fictitious ranges (`07700 900000`–`07700 900999` mobile,
`01632 960000`–`01632 960999` landline). Email: RFC 2606 reserved domains
(`@example.com`, `@example.org`, `@example.net`).
